  "title": "Grumpy Bookstore Owner",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Sliding window",
  "patterns": [
    "sliding window",
    "fixed-size window"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "the customers on non-grumpy minutes are satisfied no matter what you do with the technique. what's the only thing the technique's placement actually affects?",
    "separate the problem: a fixed total of already-satisfied customers, plus the extra customers you can 'rescue' from a grumpy stretch by placing the technique there",
    "the customers rescued by placing the technique on a window of size `minutes` is just the sum of customers[i] for grumpy minutes inside that window - a fixed-size sliding window sum",
    "slide that window across the array, tracking the maximum rescued sum, then add it to the fixed base of already-satisfied customers"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "adding customers from non-grumpy minutes into the 'rescued' sum, double-counting them",
    "recomputing the rescued sum from scratch at every window position instead of sliding it incrementally",
    "forgetting to add the fixed base of always-satisfied customers to the final answer"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A bookstore owner has customers arriving over a series of minutes.\nYou're given how many customers arrive each minute, and for each minute\nwhether the owner is grumpy (1) or not (0). Customers are only satisfied\nif the owner isn't grumpy that minute. The owner can use a special\ntechnique to stay not-grumpy for exactly `minutes` consecutive minutes,\nonce.\n\n**Return the maximum number of customers that can end up satisfied.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "n == customers.length == grumpy.length",
      "1 <= minutes <= n <= 2 * 10^4",
      "0 <= customers[i] <= 1000",
      "grumpy[i] is 0 or 1"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "the owner is never grumpy (technique doesn't matter)",
      "the owner is grumpy the entire time",
      "minutes equals the total number of minutes"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
